### Step 3B: Test Booking Approval Authorization
### Tests: only the assigned motard can approve their bookings

### ========================================
### SETUP: Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5256
@bookingId = e0106bdc-956f-492d-a496-af96d800c9de

### ========================================
### Test 1: Login as motard1 (tour creator/assigned motard)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "motard1",
  "password": "pass"
}

### ========================================
### Test 2: Login as participant1 and create a booking request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant1",
  "password": "pass"
}

### Test 3: Create a booking request (as authenticated participant1)
# After running this, manually copy the bookingId from the response
# and update the @bookingId variable at the top of this file
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "a6129bbd-a561-418e-a545-efa9cf269e0e",
  "tourMotardId": "30a00ba8-4e70-4ccd-8d18-c31cca9ce263",
  "costSharingOptIn": true,
  "emergencyContact": "Jane Doe, 555-9999"
}

### ========================================
### Test 4: Try to approve booking without authentication (should fail 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "motardNotes": "Anonymous approval attempt"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### ========================================
### Test 5: Login as participant1 and try to approve (should fail 403 - wrong role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant1",
  "password": "pass"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "motardNotes": "Participant trying to approve"
}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden (not a Motard)

### ========================================
### Test 6: Login as motard2 (different motard, not assigned to this booking)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "motard2",
  "password": "pass"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "motardNotes": "Wrong motard trying to approve"
}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden (not the assigned motard)

### ========================================
### Test 7: Login as motard1 (correct assigned motard) and approve
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "EmailOrUsername": "motard1",
  "password": "pass"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "motardNotes": "Approved by assigned motard"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with approved booking

### ========================================
### Test 8: Verify the current authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### ========================================
### Test 9: Get all bookings to see the approved status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
